      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>THE PURPOSE OF BLAST 4 KIDS IS TO PROVIDE REDUCED-COST BEFORE AND AFTER SCHOOL CARE, ACADEMIC ASSISTANCE, AND CHARACTER-BUILDING ENRICHMENT PROGRAMS TO CHILDREN IN AT-RISK HOUSEHOLDS. THESE FAMILIES FACE CHALLENGES FINDING AFFORDABLE CHILDCARE DUE TO THEIR LIMITED INCOME.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>BEFORE &amp; AFTER SCHOOL CARE (60% OF TIME): VOLUNTEERS AND STAFF HELP 48 CHILDREN WITH THEIR HOMEWORK, LISTEN TO CHILDREN READ ALOUD, AND GIVE EXTRA ATTENTION TO MATH AND SCIENCE LESSONS. ONCE A WEEK AN ART INSTRUCTOR, A ROBOTICS CLUB AND READING PROGRAM VOLUNTEERS COME TO THE SITE AND PROVIDE ENRICHMENT PROGRAMS TO THE CHILDREN.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>92396</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>SUPPLEMENTAL SERVICES (30% OF TIME): ADDITIONAL ASSISTANCE IS GIVEN TO OVER 40 FAMILIES AS NEEDED IN THE FORM OF FOOD, PERSONAL CARE ITEMS, CLOTHING, ANGEL TREE CHRISTMAS GIFTS, AND HOLIDAY GROCERY GIFT CARDS. DONATIONS OF THESE ITEMS ARE SECURED FROM BUSINESSES, INDIVIDUALS AND CHURCHES IN THE COMMUNITY. FOOD IS DONATED BY LOCAL RESTAURANTS AND THE FOOD BANK.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>0</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>SPECIAL EVENTS (10% OF TIME): SPECIAL EVENTS INCLUDE SUMMER CAMP,SEASONAL OUTINGS, CELEBRATION PARTIES AND OTHER FUN ACTIVITIES. THERE IS ALSO AN ANNUAL THANKSGIVING DINNER AND CHRISTMAS DINNER WHERE THE THEME IS VOTED ON BY THE KIDS; IT'S OFTEN NOT WHAT WOULD BE CONSIDERED TRADITIONAL; ONE YEAR THE CHILDREN REQUESTED CHINESE FOOD FOR THANKSGIVING.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
